WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.870
While the live-action Mulan contains plenty
for both kids and adults to enjoy, some elements

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.500
of the film will only be noticed by adults.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.510
From symbolic imagery to systemic societal
issues, here are some of the things only adults

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.080
notice in Mulan.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.930
As Mulan prepares to meet with the village
matchmaker, her mother helps her get dressed

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.490
and paints her face.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:26.130
During this "getting ready" sequence, we see
a number of laces and ribbons being tied tight

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:32.000
as Mulan grimaces, showing clearly how constricting
she finds not only the clothing but the entire

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.000
affair.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.050
When she emerges, she comments to her sister
that the getup completely prevents her from

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.110
expressing herself.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:46.040
"This is my sad face, this is my curious face,
and now I'm confused."

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.899
This isn't the only time that binding imagery
is used to convey Mulan having to suppress

00:00:50.899 --> 00:00:52.510
who she really is.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:56.830
Most notably, she has to bind her chest in
order to pass as a male soldier.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:01:02.210
Later the removal of those bindings help symbolize
the "death" of her male alter ego, Hua Jun,

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:06.130
and the emergence of Hua Mulan as her true
self.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:10.950
Once she embraces her identity, she undoes
the bindings of her armor and hair ties.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:14.530
Kids will pick up on the idea that Mulan is
shedding a false sense of who she was supposed

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:19.060
to be, but adults are more likely to notice
that binding has been a recurring theme since

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.700
the very beginning of the movie, symbolizing
not just Mulan's internal struggle but the

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.150
external pressures of what society determines
women should be.

00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:32.820
Mulan also makes frequent use of shadows,
reflections, and other ways of showing characters

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.570
indirectly to illustrate how they struggle
with identity.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:41.110
Many of these devices factor prominently into
how Xianniang is portrayed, and in showing

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:44.560
Mulan's journey to becoming a self-actualized
warrior.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.829
For Xianniang, whose life has taught her that
her choices are to either hide who she is

00:01:48.829 --> 00:01:53.060
or be shunned by society, we frequently see
her through smoke and shadows.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:58.040
Meanwhile, Mulan is often shown in reflections,
which highlights the incongruity between the

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:03.100
person she feels she is on the inside and
the image she has to project on the outside.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:07.409
For much of the film, when Mulan looks at
herself, her reflection wars with her own

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:09.259
perception of who she is.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:13.279
The choice to frequently portray the film's
two most powerful female characters through

00:02:13.279 --> 00:02:17.689
indirect means helps convey their internal
struggles with self-image and their fears

00:02:17.689 --> 00:02:19.799
of showing the world who they truly are.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:25.909
Kids probably won't think to question Mulan's
unswerving devotion to the Emperor and his

00:02:25.909 --> 00:02:31.180
dynasty, but adult viewers may wonder if Mulan's
cause is quite as just as she believes.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:35.510
After Mulan is banished from her regiment,
Xianniang tries to explain to her that the

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:39.620
society in which they live has no room for
powerful women like them.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:44.299
Together, she hopes she and Mulan may be able
to create a new society that won't reject

00:02:44.299 --> 00:02:45.299
them.

00:02:45.299 --> 00:02:49.709
However, Mulan doesn't even seem to consider
what Xianniang is saying, and she rushes off

00:02:49.709 --> 00:02:52.879
to save the Emperor from Böri Khan's attack.

00:02:52.879 --> 00:02:57.650
As a matter of fact, Mulan never once seems
to interrogate the idea of what unquestioning

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:02.140
fealty to the current system means for people
like her, even though she previously felt

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.230
stifled by that very system.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:07.920
The Emperor seems like a nice enough guy,
but it wouldn't be unreasonable to wonder

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.400
whether we should really be rooting for Mulan
to safeguard his dynasty.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:17.769
Granted, the 1998 film also never questions
the governmental structure Mulan vows to uphold,

00:03:17.769 --> 00:03:22.459
but in 2020, it seems like a little healthy
introspection may have been both warranted

00:03:22.459 --> 00:03:23.459
and welcome.

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:28.120
As it stands, it seems a little alarming that
Mulan fights so hard to maintain a status

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:32.889
quo that grants tremendous power to men of
a certain bloodline, while keeping women as

00:03:32.889 --> 00:03:34.349
a subservient class.

00:03:35.349 --> 00:03:39.279
While Mulan makes friends with all her fellow
soldiers, adults won't be able to miss that

00:03:39.279 --> 00:03:44.479
the looks Honghui is giving Hua Jun contain
far more than brotherly affection.

00:03:44.479 --> 00:03:49.589
Fans who interpreted Li Shang as bisexual
in the 1998 film will likely pick up on the

00:03:49.589 --> 00:03:51.590
same energy in Honghui.

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:56.359
Although it's possible Honghui suspected that
Mulan was female all along, the simpler explanation

00:03:56.359 --> 00:03:59.540
is that Honghui was simply attracted to Hua
Jun.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:04.269
His demeanor toward Mulan remains much the
same after her true identity is revealed,

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:07.140
implying that his attraction was never tied
to her gender.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:11.079
It remained constant whether she was Hua Jun
or Hua Mulan.

00:04:12.521 --> 00:04:17.310
Mulan contains a number of impressive battle
sequences, but none of the foes Mulan faces

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:21.949
loom nearly as large as the sexism she encounters
in every facet of life.

00:04:21.949 --> 00:04:25.259
Whether she's trying to bring honor to her
family through an arranged marriage or bring

00:04:25.259 --> 00:04:29.419
honor to her country through her skilled fighting
as a soldier, she's constantly butting up

00:04:29.419 --> 00:04:32.400
against the societal constraints placed upon
women.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:37.000
She's told that her powerful qi is a liability
for a woman, although it would be an asset

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.000
for a man.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.729
And during training, women are forbidden from
entering the soldiers' camp.

00:04:41.729 --> 00:04:47.009
"Bringing women into camp or consorting with
women in any way.

00:04:47.009 --> 00:04:50.080
Penalty: death."

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:54.790
What's more, this same sexist oppression is
what drove Xianniang to side with Böri Khan

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:56.150
in the first place.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:05:01.050
She tells Mulan that she tried to find a noble
path forward, but it didn't exist within acceptable

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:02.050
society.

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:05.860
The only options available to her were to
either ally herself with an enemy of the kingdom

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.181
or deny her own power.

00:05:07.181 --> 00:05:11.980
"The more power I showed, the more I was quashed.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:14.939
Just like you."

00:05:14.939 --> 00:05:19.110
Considering that Xianniang is instrumental
in gaining Böri Khan most of his tactical

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:24.659
advantages during the film, it's hard to ignore
that if society hadn't been so intent on oppressing

00:05:24.659 --> 00:05:27.830
women, the Emperor may not have needed saving
in the first place.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:29.090
The meaning of "true"

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:34.320
Throughout the film, Mulan is constantly trying
to embody the three pillars of virtue.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:46.020
Early on, she strives to live out these virtues
and make her family proud through restraining

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:50.730
her impulses in order to present herself well
and make a good and respectable match.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:56.289
Later, she experiences a crisis of conscience
when she realizes she can't possibly be "true"

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:58.819
while also deceiving everyone around her.

00:05:58.819 --> 00:06:02.800
Ultimately, she comes into her own when she
rejects both the societal expectations of

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:07.680
women and the pretense of being a man, and
embraces her own unique skills and identity.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.999
It's interesting that for the majority of
the film, it seems as though everyone in Mulan's

00:06:11.999 --> 00:06:17.310
life, including Mulan herself, assumes that
being "true" means to accept her place and

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.889
to stop bucking traditions and questioning
cultural norms.

00:06:20.889 --> 00:06:24.319
"You are the daughter.

00:06:24.319 --> 00:06:26.900
Learn your place."

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:31.270
If Mulan had remained a demure and subservient
daughter, everyone would've thought that she

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:34.210
was being true to the role that had been given
to her.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:38.860
But by the end of the film, we're shown that
what's actually "true" for Mulan is a path

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:41.620
that didn't even exist before she carved it
out for herself.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:46.909
While kids will likely embrace the film's
themes of self-acceptance on a surface level,

00:06:46.909 --> 00:06:51.340
adults are more equipped to unpack the complex
idea that our understanding of who we are

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.919
and how to live truthfully can evolve over
time.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:59.360
In all the promotional material for Mulan,
it seemed as though Xianniang was going to

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:01.330
be the main antagonist of the film.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:06.469
But by the end of the film, Xianniang has
seen an alternate version of herself in Mulan,

00:07:06.469 --> 00:07:10.560
and she ultimately sacrifices herself to save
the younger woman.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:15.169
Kids won't miss Xianniang's sacrifice, but
what they might fail to see is that Xianniang

00:07:15.169 --> 00:07:17.840
was never really a villain at all.

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:21.830
Xianniang tells Mulan that she joined forces
with Böri Khan because he was the only one

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:24.969
who provided a place for her and allowed her
to be who she was.

00:07:24.969 --> 00:07:30.350
But as we see before their encounter, she's
really more of a prisoner than a lieutenant.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:34.389
"Now I know, I serve you.

00:07:34.389 --> 00:07:35.620
I am the slave."

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:38.870
"And you would do well to remember it."

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:42.939
While she does Böri Khan's bidding for much
of the film, her true motivation is to create

00:07:42.939 --> 00:07:47.219
a society in which she can be accepted without
having to diminish herself.

00:07:47.219 --> 00:07:51.879
In Mulan, she sees the possibility of that
society, and she gives her life to help it

00:07:51.879 --> 00:07:53.430
come into being.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:57.871
Rather than an antagonist working against
the hero, Xianniang proves herself to be a

00:07:57.871 --> 00:08:02.090
tragic figure who was ultimately working toward
the same goals as Mulan.

00:08:03.289 --> 00:08:07.500
By the end of the film, Mulan has returned
home to her village, seeking to beg her family's

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.740
forgiveness for how she left and restore their
honor.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:14.969
But when she's reunited with her family, they're
not angry with her for leaving, but rather

00:08:14.969 --> 00:08:17.659
relieved that she finally came back home.

00:08:17.659 --> 00:08:21.470
Her father then tells her that he recognizes
that she's a warrior, and that he should've

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:23.279
seen that all along.

00:08:23.279 --> 00:08:27.949
Considering we've just seen Mulan defeat Böri
Khan single-handedly and get recognized by

00:08:27.949 --> 00:08:30.620
the Emperor, this exchange makes complete
sense.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:34.909
But what young viewers may not have quite
pieced together is that Hua Zhou wouldn't

00:08:34.909 --> 00:08:37.719
actually know about her accomplishments in
battle yet.

00:08:37.719 --> 00:08:42.219
As children, it's easy to assume that the
characters know whatever we know, but as adults,

00:08:42.219 --> 00:08:44.950
the flow of information becomes a lot clearer.

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:49.370
When her father says he sees that Mulan is
a warrior, he didn't come to that revelation

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:51.740
because he'd heard of her great feats in battle.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:55.980
Instead, it's because he finally admitted
the truth he'd always known about his daughter.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:09:00.360
It turns out that none of Mulan's accomplishments
were necessary for her father to finally see

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:01.360
her.

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:02.550
He'd known who she was from the beginning.

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:07.801
By the end of Mulan, it seems like women's
rights have taken a big step forward, with

00:09:07.801 --> 00:09:11.310
Mulan being invited to serve as an officer
in the Emperor's guard.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:15.970
But while Mulan herself has come a long way,
not much has been done for any of the other

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:17.800
women living alongside her.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:21.990
She returns home to find her sister excited
about her upcoming arranged marriage, with

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:26.529
the other women in her village still in exactly
the same circumstances as when she left.

00:09:26.529 --> 00:09:30.930
Granted, none of the other women in Mulan
have given any indication that they want anything

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:35.320
else for their lives, but that could be simply
because they never considered that other options

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:36.690
might be open to them.

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:41.190
Xianniang, the only other woman who wanted
something more than what society was prepared

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:43.760
to offer, is dead by the film's end.

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:48.570
Kids may be satisfied that Mulan herself is
able to finally lead the life she wants, but

00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:50.640
adults may wonder how much has really changed.

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:56.330
Mulan accepting her commission as an officer
in the Emperor's guard is presented as a happy

00:09:56.330 --> 00:10:00.310
ending, but Mulan likely has an extremely
hard road ahead of her.

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:04.920
Remember, the army that she's going to join
is the same one that, earlier in the film,

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:09.490
reminded its soldiers that the presence of
a woman in the camp was punishable by death.

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:14.030
Although the men who fought beside Mulan against
Böri Khan are ready and willing to accept

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:17.870
her as a warrior, there are plenty of other
men in the Emperor's guard who don't know

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:19.270
her personally.

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:23.600
They aren't all going to be thrilled at the
idea of admitting a woman to their ranks,

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:25.320
much less as a leader.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:28.980
Not all men will find it easy to let go of
the way things have always been done in the

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:32.930
past, and it's probable that at least some
of Mulan's fellow soldiers could decide to

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:37.610
make her life particularly difficult in order
to "prove" that women have no place among

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:38.610
them.

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:42.370
Mulan was able to earn the respect of her
peers once before, but that was only after

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.750
she'd previously earned it as a man.

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:49.380
Her new career as the only female officer
in the Emperor's guard will no doubt be a

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:53.440
tremendously challenging one, but we are sure
she's up to the task.

